			<!-- Section 2: The 5 Golden Rules for Wedding DJs & Music Lists -->
			<section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.8rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--fg-pencil); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; text-align: center;">
					2. The 5 Golden Rules of Wedding Music & DJ Collaboration
				</h3>

				<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;">
					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem;">
						<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--accent-red); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
							Rule #1: Cap Must-Plays at 15–20 Songs
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
							Handing your DJ a 150-song rigid playlist turns them into a glorified Spotify iPod operator. A veteran DJ's true superpower is reading facial expressions, energy dips, and age groups on the dance floor. Give them guidelines, not handcuffs.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem;">
						<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
							Rule #2: Edit First Dance to Under 3 Minutes
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
							Four minutes of slow-dancing under spotlight feels like an eternity. Ask your DJ to fade out smoothly at 2:30 or invite all wedding party couples onto the floor to join you for the second verse.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem;">
						<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #16a34a; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
							Rule #3: Respect Multi-Generational Appeal
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
							Start the dance party early in the night with cross-generational classics (Motown, Earth Wind & Fire, ABBA, Whitney Houston) while grandparents and older relatives are still energized. Save modern club bangers and heavy EDM for the final 90 minutes.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem;">
						<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #d97706; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
							Rule #4: Enforce Strict Do-Not-Play Guardrails
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
							Your blacklist protects you from awkward memories, ex-partner anthems, and overplayed line dances (Macarena, Cha Cha Slide). Instruct your DJ that your blacklist is 100% non-negotiable, even if a guest insists or offers a cash tip.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

