			<!-- Section 4: FAQs -->
			<section>
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 2rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">
					Frequently Asked Questions
				</h3>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						Should we give our DJ a Spotify playlist link or a printed music brief?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 0.95rem;">
						Both! Giving your DJ a Spotify playlist allows them to listen to the specific versions/remixes you like. However, providing a printed or PDF <strong>DJ Music Brief</strong> is essential on the wedding night because it contains exact timestamp cue notes, names for MC introductions, and clear blacklists that they can reference behind the DJ booth.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						How do we handle guest song requests without ruining our wedding vibe?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 0.95rem;">
						Instruct your DJ to use a "Filter & Curate" approach. This means the DJ politely thanks the guest for the request, checks if the track matches the couple's musical style and isn't on the blacklist, and mixes it in only if it enhances the dance floor's momentum.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.15rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						When should the DJ arrive to set up sound and microphones?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 0.95rem;">
